            <p>Erysipelas. This condition is a superficial infection affecting the upper dermis and superficial lymphatic system. Bright red erythema, elevation of the affected skin, and well-demarcated borders can help to diagnose erysipelas and distinguish it from cellulitis. Contributed by&#x000a0;O Chaigasame, MD</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="erysipelas" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
